<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST - Hungary's T-bill yields seen dropping.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Hungary's T-bill yields seen dropping.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields on Hungary's discount Treasury bills are likely to drop slightly at this weeks' auctions, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) will auction one-month treasury bills on Tuesday, three-month bills on Wednesday, six-month bills on Thursday and 12-month papers on Friday.</p>
<p>		    1-MONTH	3-MONTH    6-MONTH     12-MONTH</p>
<p>Amount on offer</p>
<p>   (bln forints)   1	     5	    12	    14</p>
<p>Previous average</p>
<p>	(pct)	22.01	 22.23	 22.4	  22.37</p>
<p>Valid bid</p>
<p>    range    20.01-23.01  20.23-22.73  20.4-22.9  20.37-22.87</p>
<p>FORECAST OF HUNGARIAN DEALERS</p>
<p>Csaba Deak - AFI Securities</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	21.99	 22.25	 22.42	 22.40-45</p>
<p>    AVERAGE	21.95	 22.18	 22.35	 22.35-40</p>
<p>Gyula Kerdo - Creditanstalt Securities</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	22.05	 22.15	 22.20	 22.20</p>
<p>    AVERAGE	22.00	 22.10	 22.15	 22.15</p>
<p>Zsolt Bango - Gog Securities</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	21.97	 22.16	 22.11	 22.07</p>
<p>    AVERAGE	21.83	 22.08	 22.04	 21.98</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
